@startuml
title Expire or end a private application session
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
 BorderColor #344054
 FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
 BorderColor #667085
 FontColor #101828
 BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Library owner" as owner
box "Frontend - Loupe application / api" #E0F2FE
 participant "LibraryShell / draft guard" as shell
 participant "SessionService" as client
end box
box "Backend - Loupe API application" #D1FADF
 participant "Session middleware / SessionsController" as api
end box
box "Backend - Loupe Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
 participant "ValidateSessionQueryHandler / SignOutCommandHandler" as handler
end box
box "Backend - Loupe Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
 database "Shared session store" as sessions
end box
owner -> shell : Continue editing or choose Sign out
shell -> client : Authenticated request / protected sign-out
client -> api : HTTPS with opaque session cookie
api -> handler : Validate elapsed boundaries / dispatch sign-out
handler -> sessions : Load current nonrevoked session
sessions --> handler : Creation and last activity times
alt idle >= 30 min or absolute age >= 12 h
 handler --> api : 401 expired [L2-037]
 api --> client : Safe reauthentication state
 client --> shell : Suspend draft in current-tab memory [L2-043]
 note over shell : Restore only after same owner signs in; different owner clears it
else explicit Sign out
 handler -> sessions : Revoke server session before acknowledgment
 sessions --> handler : Revoked
 handler --> api : Success and cookie removal
 api --> client : Sign-out acknowledged
 client --> shell : Clear drafts, signals, cached private objects, pending requests
else still valid immediately before both boundaries
 handler --> api : Valid session; authorize owned request
 api --> client : Owned response with private no-store policy
end
shell --> owner : Library or sign-in; Back/replayed session cannot bypass revocation
@enduml
